CORE
main.c
--add-library --dump-c _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^  return __CPROVER_sqrtf\(x, __CPROVER_rounding_mode\);$
^  return __CPROVER_sqrtld\(x, __CPROVER_rounding_mode\);$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
return sqrtf?l?\(
--
The library models of sqrtf and sqrtl must be dumped using the CPROVER built-in
rather than a call to the function itself, which would make them recursive.
